{"name":"Punk Rock Purple","hex":"#bb11aa","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"punk","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["One who engages in sexual intercourse, particularly:\n A female prostitute. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A female prostitute. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Worthless, contemptible, particularly","Bad, substandard."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/punk"},{"term":"rock","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A formation of minerals, specifically:\n  The naturally occurring aggregate of solid mineral matter that constitutes a significant part of the earth's crust.","The naturally occurring aggregate of solid mineral matter that constitutes a significant part of the earth's crust."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To pelt with rocks; to stone."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rock"},{"term":"purple","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colour between red and blue; violet, though often closer to magenta.","Any non-spectral colour on the line of purples on a colour chromaticity diagram or a colour wheel between violet and red."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a purple hue.","Not predominantly red or blue, but having a mixture of Democrat and Republican support."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/purple"}],"entries":[{"title":"Punk rock","blocks":[{"text":"Punk rock is a genre of rock music that emerged in the mid-1970s. Rooted in 1950s rock and roll and 1960s garage rock, punk bands rejected the overproduction and corporate nature of mainstream arena rock. They typically produce short, fast-paced songs with rough, stripped-down vocals and instrumentation, and anti-establishment themes. Artists also embraced a DIY ethic, with many bands self-producing and distributing recordings through independent labels."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Punk_rock"},{"title":"Purple","blocks":[{"text":"Purple is a color similar in appearance to violet light. In the RYB color model historically used in the arts, purple is a secondary color created by combining red and blue pigments. In the CMYK color model used in modern printing, purple is made by combining magenta pigment with cyan pigment, black pigment, or both. In the RGB color model used in computer and television screens, purple is created by mixing red and blue light in order to create colors that appear similar to violet light. According to color theory, purple is considered a cool color."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Iris_sanguinea_cultivar%2C_Wakehurst_Place%2C_UK_-_Diliff.jpg/330px-Iris_sanguinea_cultivar%2C_Wakehurst_Place%2C_UK_-_Diliff.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Purple"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Punk-27947.jpg/330px-Punk-27947.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Punk-27947.jpg/330px-Punk-27947.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"1980s punks with leather jackets and dyed mohawk hairstyles","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APunk-27947.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Iggy-Pop_1977.jpg/500px-Iggy-Pop_1977.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Iggy-Pop_1977.jpg/500px-Iggy-Pop_1977.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Iggy Pop, sometimes referred to as the \"godfather of punk.\"[70]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIggy-Pop_1977.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/The_Kingsmen_1966.jpg/500px-The_Kingsmen_1966.jpg?u